  "recipe_vars": {
    "{from}": "the outgoing shot's file (the clip that plays before the cut)",
    "{from_in}": "seconds into {from} at the scene's first frame: the outgoing shot's out-point minus 0.233 s (its last 7 frames are the punch). On the 30 fps grid, written rounded down to 4 decimals (frame 37 = 1.2333).",
    "{to}": "the incoming shot's file (the clip that plays after the cut)",
    "{to_in}": "seconds into {to} at the cut: the incoming shot's in-point (its media start). Same writing as {from_in}.",
    "{window}": "assets/transitions/SCENE_ID.mp4 in the project"
  },
  "placement": "Run the recipe from the project folder. Keep the project's own footage as a plain hard cut at `at` (outgoing shot until `at`, incoming shot from `at` at its in-point) and mount this scene above it with make_scene --start <at - 0.233>. Then write the host's data-start at full precision (k/30, e.g. 1.4333333333333333): make_scene rounds it to 3 decimals, and a start rounded up (1.367 for 41/30) shows the window a frame late. Outside the scene the project's own clips play and join the baked frames seamlessly, as long as both shots start at timestamp 0 (ffprobe start_time): a shot that starts at 0.033 plays a frame late in HyperFrames but not in ffmpeg, so re-time it to 0 first. The window uses the outgoing shot only up to `at` (`tail` 0); the incoming shot must last at least the window.",
  "source": "algrow-gta-pipeline/lab/transitions/tools/trans.sh zoom, 7 + 9 frames (validated as trans-E: out/trans_E.mp4, aerial > hook_beach)",
  "changed": "The lab baked whole clips (shot, move, shot) in one ffmpeg run. The template bakes only the 16 frames of the move, with the lab's exact filter graph, from the project's own two shots, and plays them over the project's own hard cut. Same frames, same timing."
